00:11:24.000 --> 00:12:15.000
LeBor had a limited view of the self to just the individual self. And his assumption was that if you lose the individual self, there's nothing left. What seems to be going on, rather, is what happens in crowds is that people shift from the personal self to the social self or social identity, from I to we. And they start acting in terms of the norms and the values of the group. So it's not that you lose identity and lose control, you shift control to the norms and values of the group. Now, certainly some groups have got appalling, pernicious values. You know, Nazi crowds, you know, genocidal, anti-Semitic, authoritarian and so on.
勒庞对自我的看法仅限于个人自我，视野十分有限。他的假设是，如果你失去了个人自我，那就一无所有了。相反，似乎正在发生的是，在人群中发生的事情是人们从个人自我转变为社会自我或社会认同，从“我”转变为“我们”。他们开始根据群体的规范和价值观行事。所以并不是说你失去了身份认同和失去了控制，而是你将控制权转移到了群体的规范和价值观上。当然，有些群体的价值观极其糟糕、恶劣。你知道，纳粹人群，你知道的，种族灭绝的、反犹太主义的、威权主义的等等。

